{
  "note": "Small extracts of official DOSM labour statistics via the data.gov.my open API: national salaries & wages (and number of wage recipients, in thousands) by MASCO major occupation group, skills-related underemployment of tertiary-educated workers, and Pulau Pinang's quarterly labour force and annual wage figures. In HalaTuju they can serve only as a coarse demand/context prior, e.g. the multi-year trend in recipients and median wage for the 'clerical' group (where an accounts-payable clerk sits) versus 'professionals'/'technicians' (where analyst roles sit), plus Penang wage and unemployment context for the demo persona. Limits: MASCO major groups are far coarser than our 16 catalogue occupations (e.g. ESG analyst, data analyst and procurement roles all fall inside broad groups), wage-recipient counts are employment stocks of citizen employees, not vacancies or hiring demand, and no occupation-by-state breakdown is published in these datasets.",
  "licence": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) - each dataset page states: 'This data is made open under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0).' Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ (statement shown on e.g. https://open.dosm.gov.my/data-catalogue/wages_occupation). Source: Department of Statistics Malaysia (DOSM), via OpenDOSM / data.gov.my.",
